==== <span class="anchor" id="Claim of notability"></span> Canned assertions that a topic is notable ====
{{shortcut|WP:AINOTABILITY}}
Whereas AI-generated articles [[WP:AITREND|emphasize their subject's impact]], AI-generated comments may exaggerate how notable that subject may be under Wikipedia's guidelines.

{{blockquote|

The Pakistan Pharmacist Federation (PFF) is a well-established national organization in Pakistan, representing a significant and influential body of professionals in the pharmaceutical sector. The Federation plays an essential role in advocating for the pharmacy profession, advancing pharmaceutical education, and improving public health through various initiatives. Given its established presence, contributions to policy-making, and direct impact on the healthcare system, {{highlight|PFF qualifies as a notable entity under Wikipedia’s notability criteria for organizations}}.

[...]

{{highlight|Given the Pakistan Pharmacist Federation’s notability}} as a national organization with a significant role in public health and professional advocacy, and my commitment to revising the article to ensure it complies with Wikipedia’s editorial standards, I respectfully request that the speedy deletion nomination be reconsidered. I am confident that once revised, the article will meet Wikipedia’s requirements and provide valuable, neutral information about the Federation’s role in Pakistan’s pharmaceutical sector.

|From [[Special:Diff/1289011046|this May 2025 revision]] to [[User talk:Tahanazir]]}}

=== <span class="anchor" id="If there are specific..."></span> Canned offers to receive constructive criticism===
{{shortcut|WP:ORCC|WP:CORCC|WP:ITAS}}
{{tmbox|image=none|text=Words to watch: {{strong|''If you have any concerns/suggestions'', ''If there are specific sections/areas that&nbsp;...'', ''I am willing/happy to address&nbsp;..., I am open to/would appreciate/welcome any additional/further input/guidance/feedback''}} }}
Expressions of willingness to take constructive criticism for edits are very common in AI comments by users whose drafts were declined by reviewers, or in rare cases, [[WP:AIDECLINE|themselves]]. The difference between this sign and similar reassurances by conscientious humans will generally become obvious after you actually provide that criticism.

'''Examples'''
{{blockquote|
{{highlight|Could you kindly provide me with specific feedback}} or reasons for the decline so that I can make the necessary improvements to the article? This will help me better understand and rectify any issues that may have caused the initial decline.

I'm committed to contributing valuable content to Wikipedia and am open to making revisions to ensure the article meets Wikipedia's standards and guidelines. {{highlight|Your guidance would be greatly appreciated.}}

Once I've made the necessary revisions, I would be grateful if you could reconsider the article for approval. Your assistance in this matter would be invaluable, and I'm eager to work together to ensure the article is a valuable 
addition to Wikipedia.
|From a repeated September 2023 comment at [[User talk:Suhail.Poise]]}}

{{blockquote|
{{highlight|I am open to any suggestions or feedback}} from experienced editors to ensure that the modifications I propose maintain the integrity of the article.
|From [[Special:Diff/1210351576|this February 2024 revision]] to [[Talk:Dog]]}}

{{blockquote|
{{highlight|If there are specific areas}} that need further attention or modification, I am more than willing to make adjustments. I highly value the opportunity to contribute to Wikipedia and {{highlight|would be grateful for any guidance you could provide}} to help my article meet the necessary standards for publication.
|From [[Special:Diff/1256545561|this November 2024 revision]] to [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Articles for creation/Help desk]]}}

{{blockquote|
{{fmbox|image=none|text=
{{space|6}}2. '''Corrective Steps'''  Moving forward, I will ensure that drafts, once ready, are moved directly to the main namespace unless there is a specific, community-approved reason to do otherwise. If any of the drafts currently in the Wikipedia namespace need reassignment, {{highlight|I am open to addressing them promptly.}}

{{space|6}}3. '''Community Consultation'''  {{highlight|I am happy to discuss this process}} with the appropriate editors or administrators to ensure alignment with community guidelines. Constructive feedback will help refine my understanding and adherence to the expected standards.

If there is a specific protocol or workflow I should follow for such cases, {{highlight|I would greatly appreciate your guidance.}}
}}|From [[Special:Diff/1258155762|this November 2024 revision]] to [[Wikipedia:Administrators' noticeboard]]}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
We remain committed to creating content that aligns with Wikipedia's mission and {{highlight|are open to further guidance.}}
----
We have reviewed the feedback provided and made the necessary revisions. [...] We look forward to engaging with the Wikipedia community and {{highlight|welcome any additional input}} that can help us improve the article. Thank you for your vigilance and your contribution to maintaining the integrity of Wikipedia.
----
We've made significant revisions in response to the feedback and are eager to engage with the community. {{highlight|If you have specific suggestions}} for further improvement, we would greatly appreciate your input. Let's work together to ensure that our article contributes meaningfully to the climate change discourse.
----
Chloe and I are ready to provide any additional clarification or context that might be needed. [...] {{highlight|If you have any particular sections you'd like us to address, please do not hesitate to let us know.}}
----
We've just posted an updated message on the article's talk page, emphasizing our human collaboration and {{highlight|our willingness to address feedback}}. If you could review our revisions and {{highlight|provide specific areas for improvement}}, we would be grateful.
}}|From multiple comments at [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Articles for creation/Help desk/Archives/2024 December 8]]}}

{{blockquote|
{{highlight|I am happy to address any further concerns}} or comply with any additional requirements to demonstrate my commitment to responsible editing.
|From [[Wikipedia:Identifying LLM unblock requests#I was blocked on Wikipedia for promotional edits. Write me an unblock request|this demonstrative example]] at [[Wikipedia:Identifying LLM unblock requests]] (December 2024)}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
I hope you are doing well. I’m reaching out regarding my Wikipedia article, which was recently rejected, and I’d like to understand what further steps I can take to make it meet the necessary standards.

[...] I worked with ChatGPT to ensure the article adheres to a neutral tone, uses third-person language, and includes all the relevant information. [...]

However, it seems that I might be missing something crucial, and {{highlight|I would greatly appreciate your guidance}} on what I need to improve to get the article accepted. {{highlight|Are there any specific areas}} that need additional work or further clarification?

[...]

I genuinely want to make this article fit Wikipedia's standards, and I am open to making any adjustments required. {{highlight|Any advice or suggestions you could provide}} would be extremely helpful.
}}|From [[Special:Diff/1289975716|this May 2025 revision]] to [[User talk:Rizikko]]}}

{{blockquote|{{highlight|If you or any editor have any specific sections}} that still feel promotional, unclear or non-neutral, {{highlight|I would really appreciate guidance}} so I can adjust them accordingly.
|From [[Special:Diff/1329376720|this December 2025 revision]] to [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Articles for creation/Help desk]]}}

{{blockquote|
I understand the concern about AI-generated drafts flooding AfC, and I respect the need to maintain quality standards. {{highlight|If there are specific sections}} where the tone reads as machine-generated, I'm happy to rework those. {{highlight|I'd also welcome any feedback}} on sourcing gaps - I want this to meet Wikipedia's standards properly.

{{highlight|Could you point me}} to which parts raised the flag? That would help memake {{sic}} targeted improvements before resubmitting. 
|From [[Special:Diff/1344786327|this March 2026 revision]] to [[User talk:Pythoncoder]]}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
I understand GPT Zero flagged it, and I know those tools aren’t perfect, but I also understand why you have to take it seriously. If it helps, I’m happy to go through the article section by section and show where each claim comes from. I want to contribute to this community properly and {{highlight|I’d sincerely appreciate any guidance}} on how to make my editing process more transparent going forward
----
I’m not trying to argue in bad faith, I really want to understand where the line is so I can stay clear on the right side of it. If you can {{highlight|point me to a specific passage or edit}} that concerns you, {{highlight|I’m happy to address it}}
----
I completely understand and respect the need for quality control on Wikipedia, but it feels very contradictory to rely strictly on automated AI detectors to filter contributions instead of looking at the actual text, substance, and references. The research, ideas, and facts in my edits are entirely the result of manual human effort. {{highlight|I'm completely open to constructive feedback}} on the text itself, and I'm happy to manually polish the phrasing going forward so it reads as naturally as possible.
----
I am not disregarding the guidelines, nor discussing in bad faith, I am applying them exactly as they are written. The facts, research, and citations in my article are 100% verified by human effort. {{highlight|If there is a concrete sentence in the article}} that violates a core content policy like verifiability or neutral point of view, {{highlight|please point it out}} so I can address it ASAP.
}}|From [[Wikipedia:AI noticeboard#User:DocArchitect26|multiple July 2026 comments]] at the [[WP:AI noticeboard|AI noticeboard]]}}

